University tuition policy (plain-text source fixture)

This policy explains the tuition schedule for undergraduate students. Tuition is assessed per semester. Students must review the published fee table before registration, pay by the deadline shown in the student portal, and contact the finance office when a payment error occurs. A student may request an installment plan before the stated deadline. Approved refunds follow the withdrawal calendar and are returned to the original payment method. Late payment can place a registration hold on the student account. The policy applies to all faculties and is reviewed annually by the academic administration.
This source fixture intentionally contains enough explanatory text for the lab corpus acceptance check. It also records that scholarships and waivers are applied before the remaining balance is calculated, that official receipts should be retained, and that disputes must include the student identifier and transaction reference. Questions about exceptions are decided by the finance office under the current academic calendar.
